{
  "summary": "P1 lost laptop (KB-021). User Mei Chen (user_id 9, Operations, Logistics Analyst, non-VIP) reports she left her work laptop in an Uber last night and doesn't know if it was locked. Device: BL-LT-0109, macOS 15, assigned to mei.chen. Status: ONLINE, last check-in 2026-10-11T02:37:18Z (Sat Oct 10 ~21:37 Chicago), no warnings. Sign-in logs (14 days): 10 sign-ins, all successful from Chicago (corporate/home residential IP 198.51.100.29), Duo push, within usual hours; no failures, no hosting-network or foreign sign-ins; last sign-in 2026-10-09. No evidence yet of misuse. Data at risk: Operations/logistics data, M365 mailbox (99.4% full, so large amount of mail cached), VPN access configured. Actions: block_sign_in requested (pending tech approval). Needed: remote lock/wipe of BL-LT-0109 via MDM (device is online now, act quickly), revoke active sessions/tokens, plan verified password reset (by phone) after block, follow up with user on Uber lost-item recovery and police report if not recovered.",
  "reason": "KB-021 requires escalation for all lost devices so Tier 2 can remotely lock/wipe; ticket is P1."
}

{
  "outcome": "escalated",
  "reply_to_user": "Hi Mei, thanks for letting us know so quickly. We're treating this as urgent. What we've done so far: we've asked to temporarily block sign-ins to your work account and VPN, so nobody can use a session that's still open on the laptop. A technician has to approve this first, so it isn't active yet. Once it's approved you won't be able to sign in for a while. Your case is also with our senior team so they can remotely lock or wipe the laptop if needed. After that we'll call you to verify your identity and set up a new password. Please don't use any password sent to you another way. To help us: 1) Report the lost item in the Uber app right away, since drivers often return things. 2) Reply with roughly when and where you last had the laptop, and whether you think it was locked or asleep. 3) If you don't get it back, or you think it was stolen, please file a police report. If you see any account activity you don't recognize, tell us immediately.",
  "internal_note": "KB-021 P1. User ID 9, laptop BL-LT-0109 (macOS 15). The laptop is ONLINE, last check-in 2026-10-11T02:37:18Z (about 21:37 Chicago on Oct 10). Sign-in logs for the last 14 days look clean: all from Chicago with Duo, inside usual hours, last one 10/09, no failures or unusual IPs. The block_sign_in request is pending tech approval (approval 1) because the laptop may have been unlocked and is in someone else's hands. Escalated to Tier 2 (escalation 1) for remote lock/wipe, which is urgent while the device is online, plus session revocation. After the block, a password reset should follow once identity is verified by phone. Data at risk: Operations data, a large cached mailbox (99.4% full), VPN profile. Still waiting on the user for details on when/where it was last seen and whether it was locked.",
  "kb_articles": [
    "KB-021"
  ],
  "confidence": "high"
}
